# justjoin-scraper — credentials and defaults
#
# Copy this file to `.env` next to the scripts and fill in what you use:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is in .gitignore, along with every `.env.*` variant — `.env.bak`,
# `.env.local`, `.env.save` — because a sibling repo in this family once
# committed a `.env.hold` with a live key in it, and another was found
# holding an untracked `.env.bak` with a 32-hex key hours after going
# public. Keep them there. A secret passed on a command line is readable by
# anything that can run `ps` and lands in your shell history, which is why
# none of these has a flag you are expected to type.
#
# Precedence, highest first:
#
#     explicit CLI flag  >  exported environment variable  >  .env  >  default
#
# So a `.env` never overrides something you typed, and an already-exported
# variable (a CI secret, direnv, your shell profile) is never clobbered by a
# file you forgot to delete.
#
# Check what was picked up, without printing any secret:
#
#     python3 env_config.py
#
# Every variable below is one this code actually reads, and every variable
# the code reads is below — smoke_test.py asserts the two sets are equal in
# both directions, because a documented-but-unread variable is worse than an
# undocumented one.
#
#
# READ THIS FIRST: on justjoin.it you need NONE of this.
# ======================================================
#
# Every route this scraper reads was served, in full, to a bare datacentre
# address with no credentials at all. Measured 2026-09-18 from a netcup VPS
# in Nuremberg (AS197540):
#
#   justjoin.it/api/candidate-api/offers            200, 100 offers, 253 KB
#   justjoin.it/api/candidate-api/offers/{slug}     200, the full record
#   justjoin.it/api/candidate-api/offers/facets/count  200
#   justjoin.it/job-offers/all-locations            200, 1.8 MB
#   justjoin.it/sitemaps/active-jobs/part0.xml      200, 10,646 offer URLs
#
# ...to `curl` with no headers at all, to `python-requests`, and to `wget`.
# Sixteen candidate bot-challenge markers were counted across seven
# captures and every one was zero.
#
# So `python3 playwright_scraper.py` with an empty `.env` is a working
# command. Everything below is optional, and what each option actually buys
# is stated rather than implied.
#
# ONE EXCEPTION, and it is a denylist entry rather than a gate: a
# `Python-urllib/*` User-Agent gets HTTP 403 on both hosts. That happens to
# be what the standard library sends if you do not set one. The engines
# take theirs from the browser and the HTTP paths set their own, so nothing
# here trips over it — the note is for anyone writing a quick script beside
# this one.
#
#
# WORTH KNOWING ABOUT CAPTCHAS HERE, because "none rendered" is not "none
# configured" (CLAUDE.md §18).
#
# justjoin.it publishes its own reCAPTCHA **v2** key in the page config on
# every page:
#
#     "googleRecaptchaV2Key": "6LeTZ-ErAAAAAA_fFNEN3N575ErA7CPrGYyZX50o"
#
# The only string in the bundle that references it sits in the job
# APPLICATION form's i18n namespace ("reCAPTCHA verification failed."), so
# the widget guards submitting a CV — which this scraper never does.
#
# Measured in a live headless Chromium, seven seconds after load, on a
# rendered listing, on an offer page and on the endpoint alike:
# `window.grecaptcha` undefined, `___grecaptcha_cfg` absent, zero captcha
# iframes, zero `[data-sitekey]` elements, zero captcha scripts. The
# reCAPTCHA script is never even LOADED on the read path.
#
# So a key buys nothing here today. It is worth setting only so that a run
# is not helpless if that changes — and if it does, a v2 widget is exactly
# what `captcha_solver.py` solves, with the sitekey the page already
# publishes.
TWOCAPTCHA_KEY=your_2captcha_api_key_here

# --- Scraping Browser API (optional) --------------------------------------
# A remote Chromium you connect to over CDP, with its own exit. On this site
# it buys you a specific exit COUNTRY and no local browser to install — not
# access, which you already have.
#
#   ws://{login}-zone-scraping_browser-country-{cc}-pid-{profileId}:{password}@cb.2captcha.com:9222
#
# `country-` picks the exit country. `pid-` is a profile with persistent
# cookies and allows ONE live connection each, so the engines refuse
# `--concurrency > 1` with a CDP endpoint — use several pids, one run each.
#
# Do NOT paste a working endpoint anywhere and leave it: a profile's
# credentials live about a day, so any pasted one is stale within 24 hours
# and produces an auth error a long way from its cause. The shape above is
# what to keep; get fresh credentials when you need them.
#
# Never combine this with JUSTJOIN_PROXY: the remote browser already has an
# exit, and layering a second on top contradicts it rather than improving
# cover. The engines refuse the combination on purpose.
JUSTJOIN_CDP_ENDPOINT=ws://{login}-zone-scraping_browser-country-pl-pid-{profileId}:{password}@cb.2captcha.com:9222

# --- Proxy (optional) -----------------------------------------------------
# Not needed for access on this site, as measured above. What it IS for:
#
#   * volume. Reaching the whole board means many requests — the site caps
#     each query at 10,000 results, so covering all 19,381 offers takes a
#     run per category. Spreading those over several exits is politer than
#     sending them all from one address, and `--concurrency N` without a
#     pool sends N times the traffic from one.
#   * a specific country, if you want to see what the site serves there.
#     (It served the same offers from every exit tried — the endpoint is
#     not geo-routed — so this is for checking rather than for changing
#     what you get.)
#
# The credentials here never reach the browser's command line — they go
# through the driver's own fields. Logs keep the host and port and mask the
# rest, because which exit a run used is the point of the log and is not the
# secret. Selenium's `--proxy-server` cannot authenticate at all, so that
# engine strips the credentials and warns rather than letting you believe a
# user:pass URL is doing something.
JUSTJOIN_PROXY=http://{user}:{password}@pl.proxy.2captcha.com:2334

# --- Default target (optional) --------------------------------------------
# Saves retyping --url — though on this site you rarely need one, because
# every mode has a correct default and the filters are flags:
#
#   https://justjoin.it/job-offers/all-locations   a browsable listing. Its
#                                                  filters are read off it
#                                                  and the run is served
#                                                  through the endpoint,
#                                                  which is the route with
#                                                  pagination.
#   https://justjoin.it/job-offers/warszawa/python the same, filtered — this
#                                                  becomes
#                                                  city=Warszawa&cityRadius=30
#                                                  &categories=python
#   https://justjoin.it/job-offer/{slug}           one offer, with --mode
#                                                  offer.
#
# Do NOT point this at api.justjoin.it. That host is what the site's own
# config calls `baseApiUrl`, and it answered HTTP 503 from nginx to every
# request tried from outside — bare, with browser headers, and with the
# `x-api-version` header its own bundle sends. The route that works is the
# same-origin proxy at justjoin.it/api/candidate-api/, and the scraper
# refuses an api.justjoin.it URL with that reason rather than a generic one.
JUSTJOIN_URL=https://justjoin.it/job-offers/all-locations

# Deliberately NOT here: an output prefix. `--out` already carries a
# non-empty default, so the loader — which only fills UNSET values — would
# never see it, and the variable would be silently inert: a setting that
# looks configurable and is not.
